extends layout

block content
  h1= title

  section.intro
    p This API allows you to access different versions of the resume in PDF format.
    p The resume is available in multiple formats tailored for different purposes.
    p
      strong OpenAPI:
      |
      a(href='/api/openapi.yaml') Machine-readable spec
      |
      | ·
      a(href='/api/docs') Interactive Swagger UI
      |
      | (local Express only). Analyzer APIs need a Node runtime —
      code npm start
      | locally, or the
      code api
      | Cloud Function on Firebase.

  section.usage
    h2 Usage

    h3 Default Resume
    pre
      code GET /
      code GET /resume
      code GET /resume/default
    p Returns the default resume in PDF format.

    h3 Specific Resume Versions
    p The following versions are available:
    ul
      each version in versions
        li
          a(href=`/resume/${version}`, target='_blank')= version
          |
          | -
          code GET /resume/#{ version }

    p
      | On Express, if a requested version doesn't exist, the default resume is served.
      | On Firebase Hosting, unknown versions return 404 (no fallback).

  section.api-endpoints
    h2 API Endpoints

    h3 Resume Versions API
    pre
      code GET /api/versions
    p Returns a JSON object with information about all available resume versions.

    h4 Response Format
    pre
      code.
        {
          "versions": ["default", "technical", "executive", "creative"],
          "count": 4,
          "baseUrl": "https://yourdomain.com/resume/"
        }

    p You can use this endpoint to programmatically discover available resume versions.

    h3 OpenAPI Specification
    pre
      code GET /api/openapi.yaml
    p Canonical API contract (OpenAPI 3.1). On Firebase, served statically after
      |
      code npm run build
      | . On Express, also available at
      a(href='/api/docs') /api/docs
      |
      | (Swagger UI).

  section.examples
    h2 Examples

    h3 cURL
    pre
      code curl -O https://yourdomain.com/resume/technical

    h3 JavaScript - Download Resume
    pre
      code.
        fetch('https://yourdomain.com/resume/executive')
          .then(response => {
            if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Download failed (${response.status})`);
            return response.blob();
          })
          .then(blob => {
            const url = window.URL.createObjectURL(blob);
            const a = document.createElement('a');
            a.href = url;
            a.download = 'executive-resume.pdf';
            document.body.appendChild(a);
            a.click();
            a.remove();
          })
          .catch(err => console.error('Resume download error:', err.message));

    h3 JavaScript - Get Available Versions
    pre
      code.
        fetch('/api/versions')
          .then(response => {
            if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`API error (${response.status})`);
            return response.json();
          })
          .then(data => {
            console.log('Available versions:', data.versions);
            console.log('Total versions:', data.count);

            // Example: Create links for each version
            const container = document.getElementById('versions-container');
            data.versions.forEach(version => {
              const link = document.createElement('a');
              link.href = data.baseUrl + version;
              link.textContent = version;
              link.target = '_blank';
              container.appendChild(link);
            });
          })
          .catch(err => console.error('Versions API error:', err.message));

  section.adding-versions
    h2 Adding New Versions
    p To add a new resume version:
    ol
      li Create a PDF file with your resume version
      li Name it according to its purpose (e.g., technical.pdf, creative.pdf)
      li Place it in the /public/resumes directory
      li The new version will be automatically available at /resume/[filename-without-extension]

  style.
    body {
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #333;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    h1 {
      color: #2c3e50;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;
      padding-bottom: 10px;
    }
    h2 {
      color: #3498db;
      margin-top: 30px;
    }
    h3 {
      color: #2980b9;
    }
    pre {
      background: #f5f5f5;
      padding: 15px;
      border-radius: 5px;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    code {
      font-family: Consolas, Monaco, 'Andale Mono', monospace;
      background: #f5f5f5;
      padding: 2px 5px;
      border-radius: 3px;
      display: block;
      margin: 5px 0;
    }
    section {
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }
    ul,
    ol {
      padding-left: 25px;
    }
    a {
      color: #3498db;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
